-3af0c71b-e5c4-410c-b2fc-d5b37935f818"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0946029f3a2274b2e55a488e472ae1f936b2bf9b224c4342113c30cc7c83750d","event_uuid":"b74b8eb9-ebc9-46d1-8d4e-90a583f72e8f","position":{"commit_sha":"87cc29d59538dd96b97f9620e51119aba88bc144","position":"1787961078007185994-b74b8eb9-ebc9-46d1-8d4e-90a583f72e8f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## /rebar-debug RCA — PROVEN mechanism; classified NOT-AN-AUTO-FIX (contract decision) → ESCALATED\n\n**Investigated on current `origin/main` @ `82a0d5cd328f` in an isolated worktree. Not a duplicate of\n6fe7** — `6fe7-956f-4901-45cf` (unreal-milky-sloth) fixed the **MCP** surface only and its own root\ncause names this CLI exposure as filed separately here. This ticket is the CLI-surface sibling.\n\n### Proven root cause (runtime-reproduced, not just read)\n`rebar show <id>` default `--output json` renders the ticket dict with\n`print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))` at\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py:207`. `out` carries `created_at` / `updated_at`\n(and `comments[].timestamp`, `last_reopened_at`, `source_created_at` when present) as Python `int`\nnanosecond values from `time.time_ns()`. Python's `json.dumps` emits them as **bare 19-digit JSON\nintegers > 2**53-1**, which RFC 8259 §6 does not guarantee across implementations.\n\n### Discriminating proof (real float64 consumers, live)\nAgainst this very ticket on `origin/main`:\n```\nSTRUCTURAL unsafe ints (|n| > 2^53-1): 2\n  $.created_at = 1787860170488898642\n  $.updated_at = 1787948098205216001\nnode  -e require(...).created_at  -> 1787860170488898600   (ROUNDED, -42 ns, silent)\njq    '.created_at + 0'           -> 1787860170488898600   (ROUNDED under arithmetic)\npython float64                     -> 1787860170488898560   (ROUNDED)\n```\n`node`'s plain `JSON.parse` and `jq` under arithmetic both silently corrupt the value; only\n`int()`/`BigInt()`/jq-1.7-literal preserve it. Mechanism confirmed.\n\n### Legitimacy — NOT a straightforward defect; this is a public-contract decision\nThe current CLI behaviour is **working-as-documented**, so the not-a-bug guard does NOT unlock an\nautomatic fix:\n- **`docs/release-notes.md:22-24`** (BREAKING entry for the 6fe7 MCP fix, 2026-08-27) states\n  verbatim: *\"On the **MCP surface only**, any integer outside the JS-safe range is now emitted as\n  its exact decimal string. **CLI `--output json` and the Python library are UNCHANGED and still\n  emit integers.**\"* The integer emission here is the deliberately, explicitly scoped behaviour.\n- **`docs/api-stability.md:23`** designates `--output json` the **\"Strongest contract\"** and makes a\n  field **retype** an explicit **BREAKING** change requiring a release-notes + CHANGELOG entry.\n- **`src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json`** types these fields `[\"integer\",\"string\",\"null\"]`,\n  so a bare integer is **schema-valid** today. (Its WIRE-FORM prose prescribes the string form when\n  out-of-range — that prose is the very policy this ticket exists to extend to the CLI.)\n\nThe exposure is a **real interoperability hazard** (silent float64 rounding on the surface where\nusers are explicitly invited to pipe rebar JSON into jq/node), but whether the CLI *should* switch\ninteger→decimal-string is a consumer-visible BREAKING **retype across CLI/library/MCP surfaces** —\nexactly the cross-surface contract/vocabulary decision the acceptance criteria call for\n(\"Decide and record the policy...\"). Per the /rebar-debug not-a-bug guard, that is handed to a\nhuman, not auto-landed. **No code changed; nothing pushed to Gerrit.**\n\n### Recommended disposition (for the human decision)\n**Option A (recommended): adopt the schema's WIRE-FORM string on CLI too.** Route\n`rebar show`/`list`/`ready`/`search`/etc. `--output json` through the existing, proven MCP seam\n`js_safe_result` (`src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py:152`, guard installed by `install_js_safe_guard`), so\nout-of-JS-range integers become exact decimal strings. This makes the single canonical schema's\nWIRE-FORM contract literally true on the \"strongest contract\" surface and closes the hazard.\nCompatibility mirrors the already-accepted MCP change: consumers coercing with `int()`/`BigInt()`\nare unaffected (`int(\"123\")==int(123)`); only naive `Number(x)`/raw-int consumers change — and they\nwere already reading corrupted values. Record it by extending the `docs/release-notes.md` entry from\n\"MCP surface only\" to \"CLI `--output json` too\", plus CHANGELOG, and add CLI regression coverage +\na structural guard so the surface cannot drift.\n- **Option B:** keep bare integers and prominently document the jq/`Number` hazard (docs-only).\n- **Option C:** add an opt-in flag (e.g. `--js-safe`) — most conservative, adds surface area.\n\nI recommend **A**: it removes a silent data-corruption footgun and unifies the three surfaces behind\none canonical schema, at a compatibility cost identical to the MCP change already shipped.\n\n### Attribution\nNot attributed (`caused_by` intentionally unset): the not-a-bug guard classifies this as an\nintended-behaviour/contract decision, not a `defect`/`incomplete-implementation`, so there is no\nescaped defect to attribute. For lineage only: the split-surface exposure was scoped this way by the\n6fe7 MCP fix (`unreal-milky-sloth`), which this ticket already records via `discovered_from`.\n\n### Sibling / parity census (Step 7) — no new work\nMCP = fixed (6fe7); **CLI = this ticket (escalated)**; Python library facade = N/A (returns Python\narbitrary-precision ints, no JSON boundary); reconciler/Jira outbound = probed clean in the ticket's\nNotes. No additional live sibling surfaces found.\n\n**STATUS: ESCALATED — awaiting a human contract/policy decision (Option A/B/C). Left `in_progress`\n(claimed) rather than closed, because the resolution is a design decision, not further agent work.**","timestamp":1787948361656879001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Option A implemented (operator-approved 2026-08-28) — change pushed for review\n\nExecuted the ticket's recommended disposition: the decimal-string wire form for\nout-of-JS-safe-range integers now applies to CLI `--output json` (and `--output llm`),\nnot just MCP.\n\n### Reuse, not rewrite\n`js_safe_result` (`src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py`) and `install_js_safe_guard` are UNTOUCHED —\nchange 2336 depends on `js_safe_result` directly. The change is purely additive: a thin\n`js_safe_dumps(value, **kwargs)` wrapper beside it (`json.dumps(js_safe_result(value), **kwargs)`)\nplus imports at the CLI emitters. Nothing was moved, renamed, or refactored.\n\n### Surfaces changed — measured unsafe ints (`|n| > 2**53-1`) before → after\n| command | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `rebar show --output json` | 4 | 0 |\n| `rebar list --output json` | 2 | 0 |\n| `rebar ready --output json` | 3 | 0 |\n| `rebar sign --output json` | 1 | 0 |\n| `rebar verify-signature --output json` | 1 | 0 |\n| `rebar audit show --output json` | 4 | 0 |\n\n`search`, `session-logs`, `deps`, `summary`, `review-plan --status` and the `--output llm`\nprojections ride the same emitters and are covered.\n\n### Library finding (asked for explicitly)\nThe `import rebar` facade has **one** JSON serialization boundary, not zero: `rebar.export_tickets()`\n/ `iter_export_states()` → `rebar._io.export_ndjson` writes NDJSON with `json.dumps`\n(`src/rebar/_io/export_ndjson.py:168`). Every OTHER library read returns Python `int`s\n(arbitrary-precision, no JSON boundary) and is genuinely N/A, as this ticket's Notes said.\nExport was deliberately left unchanged here — it is a separately versioned interop projection\n(`EXPORT_SCHEMA_VERSION`) with a round-trip contract against `rebar import`, so retyping it needs\na coordinated import-side change. Measured post-fix it still reports 4 unsafe ints. Filed as\n`guilty-pusslike-wyvern` (`a8db-dc3c-983a-40b0`), linked `discovered_from` this ticket.\n\n### Schema prose\nNo schema change was needed. `ticket_state` / `common` / `sign_result` /\n`verify_signature_result` / `plan_review_status` already type these fields\n`[\"integer\",\"string\",…]` and already describe the string WIRE FORM with **no surface\nqualifier**. That prose was true only of MCP until now; it is now literally true. The\nrelease-notes claim that \"CLI `--output json` … UNCHANGED\" was the inaccurate half and is\nmarked superseded.\n\n### Evidence\nRED first: 8 tests failing for the right reason, then green. Mutation-checked twice\n(`--color=no` + explicit returncode):\n- guard disabled (`json.dumps(value)`) → 8/8 fail;\n- `str(int(float(value)))` lossy-string mutant → the exact-round-trip oracle\n  `test_show_timestamp_round_trips_exactly` FAILS, which is the point: a type-only assertion\n  survives that mutant.\n\nGates: `make lint` 0, `make typecheck` 0 (683 files), `test_module_size_contract` 4 passed,\n`check_complexity_baseline --check` `new=0 increased=0`, `scripts/probe_rebar.py` 142/0,\nfull `tests/interfaces` tier 2215 passed / 10 skipped.\n\nNote on claim: this ticket was already `in_progress` (left claimed by the parked RCA session);\n`rebar claim` refuses with \"status is in_progress, not open\", so the claim step was already\nsatisfied. No `--force` was used anywhere.\n\nLeaving `in_progress` until the Gerrit change is `Verified +1` and merged.","timestamp":1787955096864903197},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## RCA — CLI `--output json` emits ns timestamps as bare big integers\n\n**Symptom.** `rebar … --output json` renders `time.time_ns()` timestamps\n(`created_at`/`updated_at`/`signed_at`, comment `timestamp`) as bare 19-digit JSON\n**numbers** (e.g. `1787856371950409998`).\n\n**Root cause.** Those integers exceed RFC 8259 §6's interoperable range\n(`|n| > 2**53-1`). As a bare JSON number:\n- float64 consumers (`jq`, Node `JSON.parse`, Ruby) silently ROUND them — measured\n  `…409998` → `…410000`, a −42 ns drift, no error; and\n- a lossless BigInt consumer (GitHub Copilot CLI) instead DIES re-serializing with\n  `TypeError: Do not know how to serialize a BigInt` (the failure mode documented in\n  `_mcp_errors.py:140`).\n\n**Why it existed.** The MCP sibling was fixed under `unreal-milky-sloth`\n(`6fe7-956f-4901-45cf`), whose `js_safe_result` seam was deliberately scoped to the\nMCP tool-return boundary, leaving the CLI surface with the same exposure. This is a\n**pre-existing wire-shape gap / contract evolution**, not a defect-escape — the parity\ngap was an intended-scope decision at the time.\n\n**Classification.** `preexisting`; not attributed via `--caused-by`.","timestamp":1787958540110534001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Final report — Option A implemented (RED→GREEN), pushed for review\n\n**Gerrit change:** https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2351\n(`refs/for/main`, Change-Id `I1438b9ddbfc471c840044a8759331bf45b4db47d`).\nAwaiting `LLM-Review +1` AND `Verified +1`. Ticket stays `in_progress` until both\nvotes are green and the change is merged.\n\n### The fix (single choke point)\n- Added `rebar._mcp_errors.js_safe_dumps(value, **kwargs)` =\n  `json.dumps(js_safe_result(value), **kwargs)` beside the proven MCP `js_safe_result`.\n- Routed EVERY CLI `--output json` / `--output llm` store-data emitter through it —\n  34 sites across `reads_cli`, `signing`, `_commands/*`, `_cli/*`, `_engine_support/*`\n  — not only the timestamp verbs. An out-of-JS-range int now leaves as its exact\n  decimal STRING; in-range ints/bools/floats/str/null are untouched; conversion is\n  lossless (same digits, different JSON type).\n\n### Reintroduction guard (criterion 1)\n- New AST gate `scripts/check_cli_json_js_safe.py`, wired into `make lint`, FAILS if a\n  CLI emitter writes store data to stdout via a raw `json.dumps`. Sanction marker\n  `# js-safe-ok: <reason>` (mandatory reason). Self-tested in\n  `tests/unit/test_cli_json_js_safe_guard.py` (discrimination, sanction, reasonless\n  marker, unparseable-source loudness, real-tree-clean, `make lint` wiring).\n\n### Declared-int caveat (criterion 2)\n- The CLI path applies the conversion to PLAIN dicts (from `show_state`/`to_llm`/the\n  sign manifest) with NO pydantic `model_validate` afterwards, so the string form does\n  not silently revert to a bare number. Schema already types the fields\n  `[\"integer\",\"string\",\"null\"]`. Verified on the wire.\n\n### Regression test (criterion 3)\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py` (RED-first; confirmed RED for\n  the right reason before the fix). Asserts BOTH (a) `int(wire) == stored` (lossless)\n  AND (b) the wire value is a JSON STRING (the direct BigInt-serialization guard),\n  across `show` json+llm, `list`, and `sign`. Adds an end-to-end Node `BigInt`\n  parse+re-serialize assertion (self-skips when `node` is absent).\n- Mutation-tested the oracle: disabling the conversion → 5 RED; a lossy\n  `str(int(float(value)))` \"fix\" → the exact-round-trip oracle FAILS. Teeth confirmed.\n\n### End-to-end replication (real CLI subprocess)\n```\nSTORED created_at (ns int): 1787957157590831001  (19 digits)\nWIRE token:                 \"1787957157590831001\"   ← quoted string\nNode BigInt parse:          1787957157590831001  → re-serialized OK (no TypeError)\njq .created_at:             1787957157590831001  (exact; no float64 rounding)\n```\n\n### Gates (all green locally)\n`make lint` (incl. the new gate) · `make typecheck` (684 files) · complexity ratchet\n(new=0 increased=0) · module-size (all <800) · `probe_rebar` (142/0) ·\n`tests/interfaces` facades+contracts tier (1005 passed) · regression+guard suites (26).\n\n### Docs\nBREAKING (pre-1.0) entries added to `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`,\nper-surface, superseding the MCP entry's \"CLI `--output json` … UNCHANGED\" note;\n`int()`/`BigInt()` consumers unaffected.\n\n### Plan-review gate\n`review-plan` verdict **PASS** (0 blocking; 3 advisory). Advisory on the Node-test\navailability precondition was addressed by adding the `shutil.which(\"node\")` skip guard.\nAttestation certified (`verified_at_sha 2598909d…`).\n\n### Close plan\nClose with `--class=preexisting`, NO `--caused-by`, only AFTER `Verified +1` and merge.","timestamp":1787958585997521001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## AC status — AC#3's drift protection is DELEGATED, not satisfied here\n\nRecording acceptance-criteria status explicitly, and flagging one that this change does **not**\nmeet.\n\n### AC#3 stays UNTICKED\n> \"Regression coverage pinning whichever behaviour is chosen, so the CLI surface cannot drift\n> silently.\"\n\n**What this change actually covers:** regression tests pinning **six measured commands** —\n`show`, `list`, `ready`, `sign`, `verify-signature`, `audit show`, plus `review-plan --status`\nand the `--output llm` projections. That is genuine coverage of those commands, including an\nexact-round-trip oracle that a float64-lossy implementation fails.\n\n**What it does not cover:** the clause \"so the CLI surface **cannot drift silently**\". A CLI\ncommand added *later* that emits a bare 19-digit `time.time_ns()` integer passes today by never\nbeing looked at — the never-ran class. The suite would be green because the new surface is\noutside its enumeration, not because the new surface is correct.\n\nSo AC#3 is **not** met by what shipped, and I am deliberately **not** rewording it to fit. The\ndrift protection is delegated to a new bug:\n\n- **`spherelike-oily-honeyeater` (`83eb-c3e1-3dfd-472f`)** — `scripts/check_cli_json_js_safe.py`\n  wired into `make lint`, linked `discovered_from` this ticket. Its acceptance criteria are\n  written to be non-vacuous: the load-bearing one requires the guard to **FLAG a\n  deliberately-seeded new CLI command** emitting a bare out-of-range integer, and to **PASS the\n  clean tree**. A guard that only ever passes has proven nothing. It also requires the in-scope\n  command set to be derived **structurally** from the CLI dispatch/parser registry rather than a\n  hand-maintained list inside the guard — a literal list reproduces the same drift problem one\n  level up.\n\n**Why it was split rather than added here.** This change is already at 160 non-test lines against\nthe Gerrit `bugfix-size-attestation` floor of 150. Adding a guard plus its tests would re-trigger\nthat block, and — because it would widen this ticket's recorded `file_impact` — it would **stale\nthe plan-review attestation** that the gate consumes, turning one problem into a larger one.\n\n### AC#1 and AC#2 are met by this change\n- AC#1 (decide and record the policy): Option A adopted; recorded in `docs/release-notes.md`,\n  `CHANGELOG.md`, and `docs/output-schemas.md`.\n- AC#2 (schemas + api-stability updated together, called out as a consumer-visible break): no\n  schema change was needed — the schemas already type these fields `[\"integer\",\"string\",…]` and\n  already state the WIRE FORM with no surface qualifier, so the prose became true rather than\n  changing. `docs/api-stability.md` already carries the rule and the worked example. The break is\n  recorded as BREAKING in both changelogs.\n\n### Deliberately NOT ticking the boxes in the description\nThe checkboxes are left as-authored. The plan-review attestation's signed material **pins this\nticket's description** (`material-part: description df194b5ff52c68f0 4423`), so editing the\ndescription — even only to tick a box — would stale the attestation and re-trigger\n`bugfix-size-attestation` on the open change. Status is therefore recorded in this comment\nrather than by mutating the plan. The boxes should be reconciled after the change lands.\n\n### Correction to an earlier attribution\nMy previous comment said the plan-review attestation was signed by \"a session or the operator on\nthis host\". That overstates the evidence. The DSSE principal\n`b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126` identifies the **signing environment**, not the actor, and\nevery session on this host shares it. The accurate statement: the attestation was **signed in\nthis environment** at 2026-08-28 22:57:09 UTC. I did not run the review, and who did is not\ndeterminable from the principal.","timestamp":1787959186410602740},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## PS4 — an in-repo consumer this change BROKE, and a correction to my own claim\n\nThe Gerrit `api-compat` criterion caught something I had missed: I audited external consumers\nand documented the migration, but never audited **rebar's own in-repo consumers** of CLI JSON.\nTwo existed, and this change broke both.\n\n### The consumers\nBoth parse `rebar show --output json` and type-checked the comment `timestamp` with\n`isinstance(ts, (int, float))`. A string fails that check, so the loop skips every marker\ncomment, the helper always returns `False`, and the 24h duplicate-suppression window stops\nmatching:\n\n1. `rebar_reconciler.conflict_bug_filing._recent_marker_comment` — the reconciler's conflict\n   bug filer (the one the bot named).\n2. `scripts/alert_dedup.recent_marker_comment` — shared by the `canary_bridge` and\n   `dependency_audit` alert lanes (a sibling the finding did **not** name).\n\nBoth are deliberately **fail-soft**, so the break was silent: no exception, no bad exit — just\nan accumulation comment appended on every cycle to a ticket the lane had already filed. That is\nthe same silent-degradation failure mode this whole ticket exists to eliminate, which makes it a\nfitting last catch. Both now coerce with `int()` first.\n\n**Blast radius bounded by sweep, not assumption.** I enumerated every `json.loads` of rebar CLI\nstdout across `src/` and `scripts/`. These two were the only affected consumers; the rest parse\nJira `acli`, pyright, ripgrep, the GitHub Actions API, or OSV. I also re-verified the library\nfinding rather than restating it: `_lib_reads._json_or` handles quality-gate subprocess output\nand `_lib_ops` parses a reconcile plan — neither carries ns timestamps — and library ticket\nreads remain in-process Python objects with no JSON boundary.\n\n### Correction to my earlier claim\nI stated in a previous comment that \"no schema change was needed\". That was true of the field\n**types** but **false** of one description: `sign_result.schema.json`'s top-level description\nasserted that `signed_at` is \"carried as an INTEGER on CLI/library output and as a decimal\nSTRING over MCP\" — which this change makes false. It now states the single cross-surface rule,\nand `docs/release-notes.md` / `CHANGELOG.md` are corrected to say \"no field was RETYPED\" rather\nthan \"no schema change was needed\".\n\n### Two things needing human attention\n1. **`file_impact` is now incomplete and I deliberately did not update it.** The change touches\n   `scripts/alert_dedup.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/conflict_bug_filing.py`,\n   `src/rebar/schemas/sign_result.schema.json`, `docs/output-schemas.md` and two more test files\n   beyond what is recorded. Widening the recorded `file_impact` would stale the plan-review\n   attestation (its material pins `file_impact 270d8587e151dc32 34`) and re-trigger\n   `bugfix-size-attestation` on the open change. Reconcile after landing.\n2. **Provenance:** the `scripts/alert_dedup.py` hunk and its test appeared in this worktree from\n   a **concurrent session on this host** — I did not author them. I am carrying them because they\n   fix a real consumer this change would otherwise break, and I verified them independently\n   (RED with the coercion reverted, GREEN with it, liveness case present) rather than on trust.\n   Disclosed on the Gerrit change so authorship can be attributed before submit.","timestamp":1787960850872099107},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Remediation of the change 2347 blocking `api-compat` finding (patchset 4 = a410fff2698e).\n\nThe finding was REAL, not a false positive. Sweep found TWO affected in-repo consumers, both the same shape (parse `rebar show --output json`, then `isinstance(ts, (int, float))` on the comment `timestamp`), and both FAIL-SOFT — so the break is silent, not loud:\n\n1. `rebar._engine.rebar_reconciler.conflict_bug_filing._recent_marker_comment` (the reviewer's finding).\n2. `scripts/alert_dedup.recent_marker_comment` — NOT in the review finding. This is the SHARED dedup primitive behind both scheduled alert lanes (`canary_bridge` x2 call sites, `dependency_audit`), so it is the wider blast radius of the two.\n\nBoth now coerce `int(ts)` when the value is a `str`, which accepts the integer and the decimal-string form alike.\n\nSweep basis (grep for the field names as STRINGS, not only semantic search): every `json.loads` of rebar CLI stdout, plus every `isinstance`/comparison/arithmetic use of `timestamp`/`created_at`/`updated_at`/`signed_at`/`closed_at`. Everything else is unaffected for a STRUCTURAL reason, not by luck — none crosses a CLI JSON boundary:\n- `metrics/bug_trends.py` — in-process `rebar.reduce_ticket()`; library returns arbitrary-precision Python ints.\n- `_commands/compact_plan.py`, `scripts/rebar_duration_probe*.py` — read event/sidecar files straight off disk; `signing.py`'s change touched only the stdout emitters, never the persisted record.\n- `rebar_reconciler/outbound_comments.py` — uses the timestamp only as an opaque identity key; no typecheck, no arithmetic.\n\nRegression coverage + mutation check: 4 tests in `tests/unit/test_conflict_bug_filing_js_safe_timestamps.py`, 3 in `tests/scripts/test_alert_dedup.py`. Anti-vacuity is asserted in-test (each fixture asserts its instant exceeds 2**53-1 AND that it genuinely serializes as a JSON string), plus a liveness test (a STALE string timestamp must still return False, so a coercion that degenerated to unconditional True would be caught) and a fail-soft test (junk string must not raise). Mutation-checked by reverting each coercion independently and asserting on the RETURN CODE: both mutants KILLED, each by its own consumer's test (1 failed / 16 passed in each case), and the mutation was verified to have actually applied before running.\n\nGates: `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; 30/30 on the affected suites; 3752 passed on the reconciler/conflict unit selection.\n\nAC#3 (drift protection) deliberately left UNTICKED and delegated to `spherelike-oily-honeyeater` (83eb-c3e1-3dfd-472f); no structural guard added here, and `file_impact` deliberately NOT widened, so the certified plan-review attestation stays valid. Description untouched for the same reason.\n\nNote: patchset 4 was pushed by a concurrent session working the same worktree; it carries exactly this remediation with the Change-Id preserved. The prior -1 was cleared and a fresh review/CI is pending (no vote copy — this is a code change, not `changekind:NO_CODE_CHANGE`).","timestamp":1787961078007185994}],"created_at":1787860170488898642,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"42fa7763-ef62-4fcf-a305-f280c79e304a","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6fe7-956f-4901-45cf"},{"link_uuid":"32189d9c-f7a8-446d-bd0e-04f91b4e8174","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6741-8392-1957-492c"},{"link_uuid":"a13eaad3-a199-4aae-b234-5c923636e93e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0b27-aa6d-9367-428e"},{"link_uuid":"6e26ca00-2e31-416e-b23c-08ce633bb2ac","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f70e-bb15-7dd8-444e"},{"link_uuid":"5ed49d4b-0005-4d0d-bd0f-b57aa199f1bb","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d7cd-e336-fe21-4418"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nDiscovered by the Step 7 parity census while fixing bug `unreal-milky-sloth` (6fe7-956f-4901-45cf),\nwhich fixed the **MCP** surface only. The **CLI** `--output json` surface has the same exposure and was\ndeliberately left out of that fix's scope.\n\n## Evidence (measured, structural — parsed as JSON, not grepped from prose)\n\n```\n$ rebar show <ticket> --output json | python -c '<scan for |n| > 2**53-1>'\nCLI show --output json, STRUCTURAL unsafe ints: 3\n    $.created_at            = 1787856371950409998\n    $.comments[0].timestamp = 1787856976224609473\n    $.updated_at            = 1787857168766976021\n```\n\nRFC 8259 §6 guarantees implementations \"agree exactly on their numeric values\" only for integers in\n`[-(2**53)+1, (2**53)-1]`. Any float64-based consumer of this output — `jq`, Node, Ruby, most JSON\ntooling — silently rounds these (measured −42 ns drift), and a lossless BigInt consumer (GitHub\nCopilot CLI) instead dies re-stringifying with `TypeError: Do not know how to serialize a BigInt`.\nThe CLI's public JSON output is the one surface where a user *is* invited to pipe rebar JSON into jq.\n\n## Approved remediation — Option A (operator-approved contract evolution)\n\nExtend the SAME proven `js_safe_result` conversion (already shipped for MCP under 6fe7) to the CLI\n`--output json` path: an integer outside the JS-safe range (`|n| > 2**53-1`) is emitted as its EXACT\ndecimal STRING; in-range ints, bools, floats, strings and null are untouched; the conversion is\nlossless (same digits, different JSON type). Recorded as **BREAKING (pre-1.0)** in\n`docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` — `int()`/`BigInt()` consumers are unaffected, exactly as\nfor the MCP change.\n\n### Design — a SINGLE choke point, not per-verb patches\n\nThe CLI has many scattered `json.dumps(...)` emitters (reads_cli, signing, _commands/*, _cli/*,\n_engine_support/*), unlike MCP's single `mcp.tool` seam. Rather than patch only the timestamp verbs:\n\n1. Add ONE converter `rebar._mcp_errors.js_safe_dumps(value, **kwargs)` =\n   `json.dumps(js_safe_result(value), **kwargs)`, beside the existing `js_safe_result`\n   (`_mcp_errors.py` has no heavy MCP import, so it is safe to import broadly across the CLI).\n2. Route EVERY CLI `--output json` / `--output llm` store-data emitter through it.\n3. Add an AST gate `scripts/check_cli_json_js_safe.py` (mirrors\n   `scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py`), wired into `make lint`, that FAILS if a CLI emitter\n   writes store data to stdout through a raw `json.dumps` — so a future site cannot reintroduce a\n   bare big-int. Sanction marker `# js-safe-ok: <reason>` (mandatory reason).\n\n### Declared-int caveat (handled)\n\nPer the `js_safe_result` docstring, a field DECLARED as int on a pydantic output model is re-coerced\nto a bare number by `model_validate`. The CLI path applies the conversion to PLAIN dicts (from\n`show_state` / `to_llm` / the sign manifest) with NO `model_validate` afterwards, so the string form\ndoes not revert. The schema already types `created_at`/`updated_at` as `[\"integer\",\"string\",\"null\"]`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] SINGLE choke point `js_safe_dumps`; all CLI `--output json`/`llm` store emitters routed through\n      it (not only timestamp verbs); AST guard wired into `make lint` prevents reintroduction.\n- [x] Declared-int caveat confirmed non-applicable (plain-dict path, no `model_validate`); wire string\n      does not silently revert to a bare number.\n- [x] RED-first regression test asserts BOTH (a) `int(wire_value) == stored_value` (lossless, no\n      rounding) AND (b) the wire value is a JSON STRING, not a bare number — the direct guard against\n      the BigInt-serialization failure; plus an end-to-end Node `BigInt` parse assertion.\n- [x] Recorded as BREAKING in `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`, per-surface, noting\n      `int()`/`BigInt()` consumers are unaffected.\n\n## Notes\n\nAlso probed and found clean / not applicable:\n- Library facade (`import rebar`) — returns Python ints; arbitrary-precision, no JSON boundary. The\n  `export_ndjson` helper is tracked separately as `guilty-pusslike-wyvern`.\n- Reconciler/Jira outbound payloads — searched for nanosecond integers in outbound JSON, found none.\n\nClassification: CONTRACT EVOLUTION (pre-existing wire-shape gap), not a defect-escape — close with\n`--class=preexisting`, no `--caused-by` (the parity gap was an intended-behaviour decision at the\ntime of the MCP fix).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"BREAKING user-facing entry for the CLI --output json int->string retype"},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"wires scripts/check_cli_json_js_safe.py into the make lint gate list"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"BREAKING contract entry for the CLI wire retype; supersedes the MCP entry's 'CLI UNCHANGED' note"},{"path":"scripts/check_cli_json_js_safe.py","reason":"NEW AST gate: fails make lint if a CLI --output json emitter writes store data through a raw json.dumps, so a bare big-int cannot be reintroduced"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_audit_commands.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_workflow_commands.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/_confirm.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/claim.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/composer.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/delete.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/idea.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/metrics.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/scratch.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/tracker_footprint.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/descendants.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/field_reads.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/next_batch.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py","reason":"show/list/ready/search/session-logs/deps JSON+llm emitters route through js_safe_dumps; drops now-unused import json"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py","reason":"CLI --output json store-data emitter routed through the js_safe_dumps choke point (no-op for in-range data)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py","reason":"adds the js_safe_dumps single choke point beside js_safe_result (unchanged); the exact decimal-string retype for out-of-JS-range ints"},{"path":"src/rebar/signing.py","reason":"sign / verify-signature --output json emitters route through js_safe_dumps"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py","reason":"NEW RED-first regression suite: asserts both losslessness (int(wire)==stored) and JSON-string wire type across show/list/sign"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cli_json_js_safe_guard.py","reason":"NEW self-test for the AST gate: discrimination, the # js-safe-ok: sanction, unparseable-source loudness, real-tree-clean, make lint wiring"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0b27-aa6d-9367-428e"],["relates_to","6741-8392-1957-492c"],["relates_to","d7cd-e336-fe21-4418"],["relates_to","f70e-bb15-7dd8-444e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"1afb89b6-6fd1-4386-8a84-0333a7a36499","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e127-a3ad-895a-4a2f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"CLI `--output json` emits nanosecond timestamps as bare >2^53 JSON numbers (float64 consumers round them)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1afb89b6-6fd1-4386-8a84-0333a7a36499","b503facf-2184-4816-9712-2704033bdacd","b3a1972b-5f51-4c4d-9731-607863a32d5d","b3943e92-0cc3-4b18-87c9-efc3b89f0a70","d47933e6-c6c4-4c5b-8a25-ccc7153b41b1","32189d9c-f7a8-446d-bd0e-04f91b4e8174","cdf1091c-de43-4376-b65f-dc58ac0faab1","732205ac-eb5f-4f9e-8946-a737dd405772","a13eaad3-a199-4aae-b234-5c923636e93e","775bd511-a516-405d-a941-29fccfdb86c0","ee4ac440-b568-4dba-9096-713890fa729b","f07ef6aa-4e17-46bc-bf8d-dda9d688b59a","6e26ca00-2e31-416e-b23c-08ce633bb2ac","2c2301dd-bd8b-4a21-b2b4-2e9ecb87eb9f","5ed49d4b-0005-4d0d-bd0f-b57aa199f1bb","3af0c71b-e5c4-410c-b2fc-d5b37935f818","b74b8eb9-ebc9-46d1-8d4e-90a583f72e8f"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787961078007185995,"uuid":"14fd0270-034e-469b-8658-ee59959913aa"}